homelab-developer (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release: developer.mailmasker.org, the MailMasker API reference
    (post-cutover item 49). Every ability a person or a script can use,
    118 of them by area, each with who may use it, its parameters, an
    example answer, and cURL, Perl and homelab-cli examples; every page
    also as Markdown, plus llms.txt, reference.md and reference.json.
  * A Claude Code skill, served at /skill/SKILL.md, that looks calls up on
    the site as it works.
  * Built from reference/*.yml and checked against the code at build time:
    every route reachable through homelab-api has exactly one entry, and
    each entry's "who may use it" matches the route's own access check.
  * The rule from here on: an API call homelab-cli makes is documented in
    this package first. homelab-cli's build fails on any call missing here.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 22:08:10 -0600
